  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "1) Fedora contains DC metadata with greek characters",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "2) Platform default encoding is not UTF-8",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Exceptions are thrown in proai - see ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://comments.gmane.org/gmane.comp.cms.fedora-commons.user/6026"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://comments.gmane.org/gmane.comp.cms.fedora-commons.user/6026",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The OAIProvider contains some code that uses the default encoding when converting to bytes to characters, rather than using UTF-8 (ie assuming that Fedora content is UTF-8) - see FedoraOAIDriver.java line 275).  This is causing issues when a default encoding other than UTF-8 is used.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Sample file to provoke the issue attached.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Work-around is to supply -Dfile.encoding=utf-8 to the JVM (eg add this to CATALINA_OPTS)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
