  "description": "<p>1) Fedora contains DC metadata with greek characters<br/>\n2) Platform default encoding is not UTF-8</p>\n\n<p>Exceptions are thrown in proai - see <a href=\"http://comments.gmane.org/gmane.comp.cms.fedora-commons.user/6026\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://comments.gmane.org/gmane.comp.cms.fedora-commons.user/6026</a></p>\n\n<p>The OAIProvider contains some code that uses the default encoding when converting to bytes to characters, rather than using UTF-8 (ie assuming that Fedora content is UTF-8) - see FedoraOAIDriver.java line 275).  This is causing issues when a default encoding other than UTF-8 is used.</p>\n\n<p>Sample file to provoke the issue attached.</p>\n\n<p>Work-around is to supply -Dfile.encoding=utf-8 to the JVM (eg add this to CATALINA_OPTS)</p>",
